@crew navarro-mateo
// SW5, the endgame pool (plans/ending-spec.html section 9): said only after you choose to stay. Every line is
// gated by the bare condition "endgame" (EN2 adds it to the line filter, section 22); "endgame:early" marks the
// lines that only make sense in the first two weeks after you stay (RV21).

== chat
? endgame:early
- There you are. Staying, I heard. Good. Your glove turned up, by the way. Left hand.   #funny
? endgame
- My handover note this morning said "Ordinary night." At the top. With a heading.   #funny
- Quiet shift. Board's tidy. Every spanner on its hook. That's my ordinary.
- Things turn up on the Wren. People too, sometimes. Then they stay. Glad you did.   #warm
- If you're ever up at four, I'll show you the board at night. It's very calm.

== bye
? endgame
- Off you go. Your collar's folded. There. Better.
